<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="01">
<name>Engine</name>
<section id="10007_S000L" variety="S000L">
<name>Fuel</name>
<ttl id="10007_S000L_74XT6_T00GK" variety="T00GK">
<name>Fuel Injector Assembly (2GR-FE)</name>
<para id="RM000002AAX004X" category="G" type-id="3001K" name-id="081AV-00" from="200708">
<name>Component Inspection</name>
<subpara id="RM000002AAX004X_01" type-id="01" category="01">
<s-1 id="RM000002AAX004X_01_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000F6P00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Fuel Injector Assembly</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="2">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09268-31012</s-number>
<s-subnumber>09268-41500</s-subnumber>
<s-subnumber>90467-13001</s-subnumber>
<s-subnumber>95336-08070</s-subnumber>
<s-subnumber>09268-41140</s-subnumber>
<s-subnumber>09268-41400</s-subnumber>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09842-30080</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<s2>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A116182" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.19in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.74in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.20in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1 - 2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Injector temperature 20°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>11.6 to 12.4Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Injection Volume Inspection</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Perform the inspection in a well-ventilated area and keep away from fire.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Remove the fuel pipe clamp.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Disconnect the fuel tube.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A136939" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the fuel tube disconnection procedure, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002AAT004X"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Connect SST to the fuel pipe (vehicle side).</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A160846J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>SST (connector) seals the fuel tube connector and pipe with an O-ring, so be careful not to damage the connection or allow foreign matter to adhere.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Install the O-ring to the fuel injector.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Install SST and a vinyl tube to the fuel injector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A129474J03" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09268-41140</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09268-41400</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Set the fuel injector in a graduated cylinder.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A086834J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Connect SST (EFI inspection wire H) to the fuel injector.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09842-30080</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Following the screen display, select "Active Test" - "Circuit Relay" - "ON" to operate the fuel pump.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Connect SST (EFI inspection wire H) to the battery, inject fuel (15 seconds) 2-3 times and calculate the average value.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC1" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Injection volume</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Difference between each injector</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>84 to 100 ml</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>16ml or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Always perform the switching at the battery terminal side.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If the result is not as specified, replace with a known good part.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Leak Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>In the condition above, check that no fuel leaks from the injector when SST (EFI inspection wire H) is disconnected from the battery.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A138003" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>1 drops or less / 16 minutes </ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Connect the fuel tube.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the fuel tube connection procedure, refer to <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000002AAT004X"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Install the fuel pipe clamp.</ptxt>
</s3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
